# Gijgo library

Gijgo is a set of JavaScript UI controls (widgets) built on jQuery, with themes for Material Design, Bootstrap 3/4/5, and shadcn. Each control lives under `src/<widget>/` as plain JavaScript and CSS, not a framework component.

Widgets include grid, tree, dialog, editor, checkbox, dropdown, datepicker, timepicker, datetimepicker, slider, colorpicker, draggable, and droppable. Shared code is in `src/core`.

## Where to edit

Change widget behavior, styles, messages, and examples only in `src/`.

- `src/<widget>/js/` — behavior, config, events, methods, and example markup
- `src/<widget>/css/` — styles
- `src/core/`, `src/icons/`, `src/fonts/` — shared runtime assets

`dist/` and `examples/` are generated. Do not create or edit files there. A change that only updates those folders will be overwritten on the next build.

`Gruntfile.js` is the build definition. Edit it only to register a new widget or asset in `concat` or `extractExamples`. Do not put widget implementation there.

## Build

From the repo root, after `npm install` and `npm install -g grunt-cli`:

- `grunt` rebuilds `dist/` and `examples/`, then watches `src/**/*.{js,css,txt}`.
- For a one-shot rebuild without the watcher: `grunt copy extractExamples concat clean replace uglify cssmin`.
- `node app.js` serves the generated examples at http://localhost:4000/.

Verify a control by rebuilding, then opening the generated example. Do not hand-write the HTML under `examples/`.
